{"groups":[{"members":["c1","c2","c3","c4"],"primary":"c1","title":"Berkeley Municipal Code Chapter 13.63: Prohibition on the Sale or Use of Coordinated Pricing Algorithms to Set Rents or Manage Occupancy Levels","requirement":"It is unlawful to sell, license or otherwise provide to Berkeley landlords a coordinated pricing algorithm that sets or recommends rents or occupancy levels for Berkeley residential units, and unlawful for landlords to use one; each month and each unit is a separate violation. The City Attorney and aggrieved tenants may sue for injunctive relief, damages and civil penalties, with attorney's fees to a prevailing City or tenant.","key_value":"Civil penalties up to $1,000 per violation; Competitor Data means non-public data less than 90 days old","status":"in_force","effective_date":null,"end_date":null,"citation":"Berkeley Municipal Code ch. 13.63 (Ordinance No. 7,992-N.S.)","coverage_conditions":"All residential dwelling units in the City of Berkeley and their landlords, plus sellers and providers of coordinated pricing algorithms to Berkeley landlords.","exemptions":"The definition excludes: (a) products that publish aggregated, anonymous rental data without recommending rents, fees or occupancy rates; (b) products used to set rent or income limits under local, state or federal affordable housing guidelines; (c) products or processes used for market research for project financing, appraisals, or research, testing or training for software development (including training machine learning models, provided Competitor Data is not an operational input when a recommendation is calculated).","conflict_note":"Status conflict: D001 (official) shows only a first reading ('passed to print' on November 18, 2025) and so supports 'pending'. D002, D037 and D086 report the ban as in force, and D002 notes that RealPage, Inc. v. City of Berkeley was dismissed with prejudice on Jan. 14, 2026. D001 predates final adoption, and three later sources agree, so 'in_force' is kept. Effective date: D002 and D037 give only '2026-01' (month precision). D001 gives no effective date. A full ISO date is not supported, so effective_date is left null pending verification of the adoption and effective date."}],"dropped":[]}
```
